   "Northwind-negotiator": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S2 has no sales bar above 5%, only regulator discretion, and no transition limit, which favours Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition and counts unreported incidents, so Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) must be recalled, a clear cost to Halcyon. S4's 36-month suppression start is Halcyon's preferred timing, and S3's six-year retrofit is within the acceptable range and favours Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage."
 },
